{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774275938,"nonce":"2Zxlt9d9E6jLpS7Whanu3bdmuN4=","title":"Increase lock retry count and use exponential backoff","message":"## Problem\n\n3 retries × 5s fixed delay = 15s total retry window is not enough. Long git-bug operations (pull/push over network) can hold the lock longer than 15s.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Rename `LOCK_RETRY_DELAY_S` to `LOCK_RETRY_BASE_DELAY_S = 1`\n2. Increase `LOCK_RETRY_ATTEMPTS` from 3 to 6\n3. Use exponential backoff: `delay = LOCK_RETRY_BASE_DELAY_S * (2 ** attempt)` — delays of 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32s (~63s total window)\n4. Update tests to assert exponential delays and new constant values\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `LOCK_RETRY_ATTEMPTS = 6`\n- [ ] `LOCK_RETRY_BASE_DELAY_S = 1` (renamed from `LOCK_RETRY_DELAY_S`)\n- [ ] Delay doubles each attempt: 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s, 32s\n- [ ] Tests updated for new constants and exponential delays\n- [ ] All existing lock retry tests pass","files":null}]}